<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Relic of the tooth of the Buddha</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sacred Tooth Relic</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Relic of the tooth of the Buddha is a tooth venerated in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a> as a remnant of the Buddha, said to have been brought from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalinga">Kalinga</a> in the 4th century CE. Possession of the relic came to symbolise the right to rule, so successive Sinhalese capitals, from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anuradhapura">Anuradhapura</a> to Dambadeniya and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kandy">Kandy</a>, built temples to house it. It is kept in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/temple-of-the-tooth">Temple of the Tooth</a> at Kandy.</p></div>
